# Auth and security

Sessions (see docs/adr/003-server-side-sessions.md):
- Server-side sessions in Redis; the browser only holds a random session id.
- Cookie: `__Host-sid`, `HttpOnly; Secure; SameSite=Lax; Path=/`. No `Domain`.
- Rotate the session id on every login. Logout deletes the Redis session.
- Idle timeout 7 days, absolute max 30 days.

SSO (OIDC, Authorization Code + PKCE):
- Validate `state`, `nonce`, ID token signature, `iss`, `aud`, `exp`.
- Link an SSO identity to an existing account only if the provider marks the email verified.

Passwords: argon2id. Rate-limit `/auth/*` per IP and per account in Redis.

Web: CSRF token on POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE + `Origin` check; CORS allows only the web origin with credentials; `helmet` on.

Never: tokens in localStorage, JWTs as sessions, logging passwords/tokens/cookies.
